# crystod-mol --diagram examples: molecular-orbital diagrams
# Symmetry + overlap only (default; symmetry-adapted extended Hueckel), or
# quantitative with --pyscf (three SCF calculations in one AO space).
# Every level in the HTML carries a drag-rotatable orbital sketch (hover panel).
# Run in this directory.

crystod-mol --diagram --xyz XYZ_NH3.xyz

* Molecule *
XYZ_NH3.xyz (NH3, 4 atoms)

* Point group *
C3v (Hermann-Mauguin: 3m)

* Fragments *
central atom: N; ligands: 3 H

* Valence AO parameters (single-zeta STO, extended Hueckel) *
N 2s:  zeta = 1.950 / bohr,  H_ii = -26.0 eV
N 2p:  zeta = 1.950 / bohr,  H_ii = -13.4 eV
H 1s:  zeta = 1.300 / bohr,  H_ii = -13.6 eV

* Ligand SALCs (standard point-group axes) *
-- 3H 1s --
A1: [1s(H1) + 1s(H2) + 1s(H3)]
E: [1s(H1) - 1s(H3), 1s(H1) - 2 1s(H2) + 1s(H3)]

* Ligand SALC | central AO overlap integrals *
  A1:  < a1 (E =  -16.44 eV) | N 2s >  S = 0.7205
  A1:  < a1 (E =  -16.44 eV) | N 2p >  S = 0.2387
   E:  < e (E =  -11.16 eV) | N 2p >  S = 0.5687

* Molecular orbitals (Wolfsberg-Helmholz, K = 1.75) *
    MO    E (eV)  occ  composition
   4a1     21.14    0  70% SALC a1, 25% N 2s, 5% N 2p
 2e x2      2.78    0  59% SALC e, 41% N 2p
   3a1    -13.75    2  95% N 2p, 4% SALC a1, 1% N 2s
 1e x2    -16.49    4  59% N 2p, 41% SALC e
   2a1    -28.00    2  73% N 2s, 27% SALC a1

* Electron filling (8 valence electrons) *
(2a1)^2 (1e)^4 (3a1)^2
(MO numbering counts the core shells, not shown: N 1s -> a1)
HOMO = 3a1 (-13.75 eV), LUMO = 2e (2.78 eV), gap = 16.53 eV

Method: symmetry-adapted extended Hueckel over single-zeta STOs
(exact two-center overlaps; energies are semi-quantitative).
M. Wolfsberg and L. Helmholz, J. Chem. Phys. 20, 837 (1952);
R. Hoffmann, J. Chem. Phys. 39, 1397 (1963).

MO diagram written to MolOD_XYZ_NH3.html


crystod-mol --diagram --xyz XYZ_H2O.xyz

* Molecule *
XYZ_H2O.xyz (H2O, 3 atoms)

* Point group *
C2v (Hermann-Mauguin: mm2)

* Fragments *
central atom: O; ligands: 2 H

* Valence AO parameters (single-zeta STO, extended Hueckel) *
O 2s:  zeta = 2.275 / bohr,  H_ii = -32.3 eV
O 2p:  zeta = 2.275 / bohr,  H_ii = -14.8 eV
H 1s:  zeta = 1.300 / bohr,  H_ii = -13.6 eV

* Ligand SALCs (standard point-group axes) *
-- 2H 1s --
A1: [1s(H1) + 1s(H2)]
B1: [1s(H1) - 1s(H2)]

* Ligand SALC | central AO overlap integrals *
  A1:  < a1 (E =  -15.52 eV) | O 2s >  S = 0.5970
  A1:  < a1 (E =  -15.52 eV) | O 2p >  S = 0.3096
  B1:  < b1 (E =  -10.52 eV) | O 2p >  S = 0.5074

* Molecular orbitals (Wolfsberg-Helmholz, K = 1.75) *
    MO    E (eV)  occ  composition
   4a1     10.65    0  77% SALC a1, 13% O 2s, 9% O 2p
   2b1      0.26    0  67% SALC b1, 33% O 2p
   1b2    -14.80    2  100% O 2p
   3a1    -15.46    2  91% O 2p, 8% SALC a1, 1% O 2s
   1b1    -17.13    2  67% O 2p, 33% SALC b1
   2a1    -33.27    2  86% O 2s, 15% SALC a1

* Electron filling (8 valence electrons) *
(2a1)^2 (1b1)^2 (3a1)^2 (1b2)^2
(MO numbering counts the core shells, not shown: O 1s -> a1)
HOMO = 1b2 (-14.80 eV), LUMO = 2b1 (0.26 eV), gap = 15.06 eV

Method: symmetry-adapted extended Hueckel over single-zeta STOs
(exact two-center overlaps; energies are semi-quantitative).
M. Wolfsberg and L. Helmholz, J. Chem. Phys. 20, 837 (1952);
R. Hoffmann, J. Chem. Phys. 39, 1397 (1963).

