* Molecule *
XYZ_H2O.xyz (H2O, 3 atoms)

* Point group *
C2v (Hermann-Mauguin: mm2)

* Fragments (pre-bonding states; removed atoms kept as ghost basis) *
left : H2 (H, H), spin 2S = 0
right: O (O), spin 2S = 0
(fragments are spin/spherically averaged: fractional occupation of degenerate frontier shells)

* PySCF calculations (Hartree-Fock method / def2-svp basis) *
      H2 (RHF): E_tot = -1.002688 Ha (converged)
       O (RHF): E_tot = -74.301396 Ha (converged)
     H2O (RHF): E_tot = -75.961329 Ha (converged)
interaction energy E(mol) - E(left) - E(right) = -0.657244 Ha = -17.885 eV
(counterpoise-consistent: all three calculations use the full molecular basis)

